{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1096724-bloodlines-active-in-the-camarilla","id":1096724,"title":"Bloodlines active in the Camarilla","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T08:09:46-07:00","id":1096724,"title":"Bloodlines active in the Camarilla","content":"So, I'm getting the itch to run some RfR (actually, probably a Roman era Requiem/Forsaken crossover), and I want to figure out what Bloodlines would have existed at the time, and of those, which should be available to my players. I know this question has been asked before, but rather than necro it, I thought I would start a new one, particularly because I want to focus not only on which Bloodlines would have existed during the Roman era, but also which ones would have been active in or around Rome at the time, so I can narrow down the list od playable Bloodlines. Here's what I've got so far.<br /> <br /> Included in Requiem for Rome:<ul><li>Larvae (Gangrel)</li> <li>Lincii (Julii/Nosferatu)</li> <li>Morbus (Mekhet)</li> </ul>Mentioned in Fall of the Camarilla:<ul><li>Khaibit (Mekhet)</li> <li>Macellarius (Ventrue [Julii?])</li> </ul>2e Bloodlines that would logically have existed at the time:<ul><li>Kerberoi (Gangrel)</li> <li>Neglatu (Any)</li> </ul>1e Bloodlines active in the core of the Roman Empire at the time:<ul><li>Agonistes (Mekhet)</li> <li>Alucinor (Mekhet)</li> <li>Annunaku (Gangrel)</li> <li>Anvari (Daeva)</li> <li>Empusae (Gangrel)</li> <li>Eupraxus (Daeva)</li> <li>Galloi (Nosferatu)</li> <li>Gorgons (Ventrue [Julii?])</li> <li>Gulikan (Daeva)</li> <li>The Hounds of Actaeon (Gangrel)</li> <li>Mnemosyne (Mekhet)</li> <li>Naditu (Daeva)</li> <li>Qedeshah (Mekhet)</li> <li>Telamones (Nosferatu)</li> </ul>1e Bloodlines active at the borders of the Roman Empire at the time:<ul><li>Adroanzi (Nosferatu)</li> <li>Bron (Ventrue)</li> <li>En (Daeva)</li> <li>Iltani (Mekhet)</li> <li>Lygos (Nosferatu)</li> <li>The Mara (Gangrel)</li> <li>Noctuku (Nosferatu)</li> <li>Norvegi (Bloodline)</li> <li>Vedma (Gangrel)</li> </ul>So my questions are, am I missing anything from these lists? Do any of them need revision? And, more importantly, which Bloodlines should I make available for PCs, and which ones should remain set dressing only? I'm thinking I want to include all of the Bloodlines mentioned in RfR and FotC, plus any Bloodlines with specifically Greco-Roman origins, like Kerberoi, Galloi, and Hounds of Actaeon. Ideally, it would be great to have an equal number of Bloodlines available to each Clan, but that's not strictly necessary. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-25-2017, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T21:31:17-07:00","id":1096978,"title":"","content":"Maybe one Malocusian, who's haven is some out of the way olive orchard or winery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}